    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d283">

                <pb facs="0457" n="415" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg415"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 696.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1863-09-05"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 5, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatch of the 21st of August (No.
                    479) has been received. You have proceeded very properly in communicating to Mr.
                    Dudley Earl Russell’s note, correcting what is represented as an erroneous
                    statement of the former in regard to Mr. Welsman, of the firm of Fraser,
                    Trenholm &amp; Company. Earl Russell’s note will be placed on the files of this
                    department.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
